"oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"not_legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{2}{U}{U}","name":"Turnabout","oracle_id":"715d0777-4d36-463b-9102-6bb6bb00b7e9","oracle_text":"Choose artifact, creature, or land. Tap all untapped permanents of the chosen type target player controls, or untap all tapped permanents of that type that player controls.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2023-01-13","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":["G"],"colors":["G"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"banned","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"banned","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{G}","name":"Veil of Summer","oracle_id":"002965be-a36f-4a09-9ce0-c6535bca1703","oracle_text":"Draw a card if an opponent has cast a blue or black spell this turn. Spells you control can't be countered this turn. You and permanents you control gain hexproof from blue and from black until end of turn. (You and they can't be the targets of blue or black spells or abilities your opponents control.)","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2019-07-12","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"A spell or ability that counters spells can still target your spells after Veil of Summer resolves. When that spell or ability resolves, your spell won't be countered, but any additional effects of the countering spell or ability will still happen.","oracle_id":"002965be-a36f-4a09-9ce0-c6535bca1703","published_at":"2019-07-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If your opponents have cast more than one blue or black spell, you still draw only one card as Veil of Summer resolves.","oracle_id":"002965be-a36f-4a09-9ce0-c6535bca1703","published_at":"2019-07-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Veil of Summer has no effect until it resolves. It can be countered.","oracle_id":"002965be-a36f-4a09-9ce0-c6535bca1703","published_at":"2019-07-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You decide on resolution if you are tapping or untapping, and which kind of permanent you are affecting.","oracle_id":"715d0777-4d36-463b-9102-6bb6bb00b7e9","published_at":"2022-12-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Although Darksteel Citadel is an artifact, it can't be cast as a spell. Playing it follows the normal rules for playing a land.","oracle_id":"8dc067bf-f78f-4ac4-b6e7-b305c42cf0bc","published_at":"2014-07-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If Dryad Arbor is changed into another basic land type (such as by Sea's Claim), it continues to be a creature and a Dryad.","oracle_id":"e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71","published_at":"2011-09-22","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Although originally printed with a characteristic-defining ability that defined its color, this card now has a color indicator. This color indicator can't be affected by text-changing effects (such as the one created by Crystal Spray), although color-changing effects can still overwrite it.","oracle_id":"e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71","published_at":"2013-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Dryad Arbor is played as a land. It doesn't use the stack, it's not a spell, it can't be responded to, it has no mana cost, and it counts as your land play for the turn.","oracle_id":"e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Due to its color indicator (appearing to the left of its type line), Dryad Arbor is green. Color indicators apply in all zones, not just the battlefield.","oracle_id":"e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Forest is a land type and Dryad is a creature type.","oracle_id":"e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If Dryad Arbor is changed into another basic land type, it continues to be a green Dryad creature.","oracle_id":"e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a Dryad Arbor gains flash, or you have the ability to play Dryad Arbor as though it had flash (due to Teferi, Mage of Zhalfir or Scout's Warning, for example), you can ignore the normal timing rules for when during your turn you can play a land, but not any other restrictions. You can't play Dryad Arbor during another player's turn, and you can't play Dryad Arbor if you don't have any land plays remaining.","oracle_id":"e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Becoming an artifact doesn't change what color(s) a permanent is.","oracle_id":"f4bdc551-c2eb-4a34-a3e3-b4a017c925af","published_at":"2011-01-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You may target any permanent with the ability, including an artifact.","oracle_id":"f4bdc551-c2eb-4a34-a3e3-b4a017c925af","published_at":"2011-01-01","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
